description: After codebase updates, push Gas-Tracker and republish GitHub Pages
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user asks to update this codebase, finish the code change, then commit and push `main`, rebuild the static demo, and push that export to `gh-pages` so https://neversmile0825.github.io/Gas-Tracker/ updates.

- Remote URL must include the NeverSMILE0825 user: `https://NeverSMILE0825@github.com/NeverSMILE0825/Gas-Tracker.git`.
- The stored GitHub credential has `repo` scope and cannot push `.github/workflows`. Publish by copying `apps/web/.next-pages` to an orphan `gh-pages` commit. Do not add a GitHub Actions workflow.
- Static export command, from the repo root:

```powershell
$env:GITHUB_PAGES='true'
$env:NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_SOURCE='browser'
pnpm --filter @gasscope/web build
```

- Do not print tokens or credential-manager secrets.
- Do not commit `.env`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `.next-pages`, or `out` on `main`.
- Do not change git config, force-push `main`, or skip hooks. Updating `gh-pages` replaces that branch with the new static export.
- The published site is the in-browser synthetic demo. Do not claim it is mainnet.
- If the user explicitly says not to push, skip the push.
